      ":question/problem": "![](images/9b/9ba7fefa5f3b3a3f90784ff23bcc54a5f60cfd4d35ac26793c1152a174c91613.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $AD^(\u2015)$ bisects both $\u2220BAC$ and $\u2220BDC$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $\u25b3ADC\u2245\u25b3ADB$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $AD^(\u2015)$ bisects $\u2220BAC$ | Given |\n| 2 | $AD^(\u2015)$ bisects $\u2220BDC$ | Given |\n| 3 | $\u2220CAD\u2245\u2220BAD$ | Definition of an angle bisector |\n| 4 | $\u2220CDA\u2245\u2220BDA$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 5 | $AD^(\u2015)\u2245AD^(\u2015)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 6 | $\u25b3ADC\u2245\u25b3ADB$ | {{field-3}} |"
